WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
The road behind me is closed.
There's been a landslip.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.140
And that's a problem because it's pretty much the only road that connects the villages of

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.180
Kelston and a dozen others besides

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:12.420
to the picturesque city of Bath.
There is a detour, but it's 14 miles long,

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.580
and the council won't be able to open this
road for a few months yet.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.660
But there is a solution, and it's quite an astonishing one.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.380
This is the Kelston toll road,

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.460
and it was set up not by the council,
but by - well - this man.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.600
MIKE: We were in the local pub one night after the road had been closed about 3 months.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.480
We were talking to the local
farmer who owns the land here.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.680
My wife suggested that he should
put down some stone and maybe

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.620
set up a toll road and charge people to go over.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:46.340
We were gung-ho. We carved the field. We built the road. We did it without planning permission.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.800
TOM: As you might expect, the council
are not initially happy about this,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.440
but here's the thing: Mike is not breaking the law.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.320
In the U.K., not getting planning permission - the U.S. translation would be violating zoning laws -

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.500
but in the U.K., not getting planning permission
is not a crime in itself.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.540
You're only breaking the law when the council notices, files an enforcement order against you,

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.940
and then you refuse to undo what you've done.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.800
MIKE: So we thought that they would say, "well
look, you know, get on and do it,

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.740
this is great, you've got our full support."

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:23.200
They - they didn't come up with that and they've actually made us apply for retrospective planning permission.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.620
TOM: The council did have some good reasons.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.200
According to their statement,

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.280
they weren't sure if construction and driving up there would affect the landslip down there.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.360
But, they seem to have taken the risk, and it's paid off.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.860
Mind you, they're not the only ones taking a
fairly big risk on this road.

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:42.760
MIKE: My wife and I have got a lovely little cottage in Kelston down by the river.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:49.280
We put our house up as a guarantee with the road builders to say, "look, we want to build this road.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:54.800
If it doesn't work out, we will sell our house and we'll pay you, and it's the only way we can make this happen.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.260
They're a local firm and they agreed to it.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:04.340
We shook hands and they sent 3 guys over and
they built this road in 10 days.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.600
We've got to get 150,000 cars over to get our money back - but we're well on the way,

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:14.080
we've had 100,000. The public's reaction has been
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE]

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.820
it has been astonishing.
The public's reaction has been astonishing.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.220
TOM: It's even made it onto Google Maps.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:22.700
So there you go.
The Kelston toll road.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.560
Something you might not have known about - not just because of its existence,

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.840
but also the fact it is still running, and it looks
like it will be for a few months yet.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.360
